==Cebuano==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ceb|poz-pro|*(i-)kita}}, from {{inh|ceb|map-pro|*(i-)kita}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ceb-IPA|kitá}}
* {{hyph|ceb|ki|ta}}

====Pronoun====
{{ceb-head|pronoun|kitá|b=+}}

# (inclusive) [[we]], [[us]]
#: {{uxi|ceb|'''kita''' ra|only '''us''', just '''us'''}}
## {{q|as the subject of a verb}}
##: {{uxi|ceb|nangadto '''ta''' niaging tuig|'''we''' went last year}}
## {{q|as the subject of a nominal predicate}}; [[we]] [[are]] 
##: {{uxi|ceb|anak '''ta''' sa Ginoo|'''we are''' children of God}}
# {{lb|ceb|with verb root|or|in the infinitive}} let [[us]], [[let's]]
#: {{uxi|ceb|adto '''ta''' / mangadto '''ta'''|'''let's''' go}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Subject (direct) pronouns are most commonly placed after the verb, or the first noun of the nominal predicate that they modify. Pronouns in this position are almost always in their short form (in this case, {{m|ceb|ta}}); the full form ({{m|ceb|kita}}) may be used to make the sentence sound more formal, or it may be placed before the verb or noun which gives the same effect. See {{m|ceb|ako}} for examples.

====See also====
{{ceb-personal pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|ceb|poz-pro|*kita}}, from {{der|ceb|map-pro|*kita}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ceb-IPA|kitá7}}
{{ceb-IPA|kita7}}
* {{hyph|ceb|ki|ta}}

====Verb====
{{ceb-verb|kitâ/kità|b=+}}

# to [[see]]
#: {{uxi|ceb|naka'''kita''' na ka sa pelikula?|have you '''seen''' the movie?}}
# to [[find]]
#: {{syn|ceb|kaplag|hipalag}}
#: {{uxi|ceb|na'''kit'''-an nako ang lapis|I '''found''' the pencil}} 
# to [[meet]] with
#: {{syn|ceb|abot|tabo|tungka|bagat|sugat}}
# to [[earn]]
#: {{syn|ceb|sapi|diya}}

=====Derived terms=====
